    {
      "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-fourth/sceneV_10.1/p@169859",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "SHALLOW.\nThere is many complaints, Davy, against that Visor. That Visor is an arrant knave, on my knowledge.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-fourth/sceneV_10.1/p@169859/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 8,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-fourth/sceneV_10.1/p@169859/line-2",
          "start": 9,
          "end": 108,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        }
      ],
      "sourceRef": {
        "start": 1867566,
        "end": 1867705,
        "line": 69766,
        "column": 1,
        "path": "chap10/p@169859",
        "anchor": "sceneV_10.1"
      },
      "speakerLabel": "SHALLOW.",
      "attribution": {
        "status": "explicit",
        "cueStart": 0,
        "cueEnd": 8
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-fourth/sceneV_10.1/p@170002",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "DAVY.\nI grant your worship that he is a knave, sir, but yet, God forbid, sir, but a knave should have some countenance at his friend’s request. An honest man, sir, is able to speak for himself, when a knave is not. I have served your worship truly, sir, this eight years; and if I cannot once or twice in a quarter bear out a knave against an honest man, I have but a very little credit with your worship. The knave is mine honest friend, sir; therefore I beseech your worship let him be countenanced.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-fourth/sceneV_10.1/p@170002/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 5,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
